      },
      {
        "factor": "Implementation timing set to commence from April 2026",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Parliamentary and government sources indicate immigration rule changes would begin from April 2026, increasing the likelihood the change appears by May 2026."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Exemptions and time-adjustments create non-uniform waits and limit the 10-year baseline for many cohorts",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Provisions include reductions (e.g., 5 years or 15 years baselines for certain routes), meaning the 10-year baseline would not apply uniformly."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Transitional arrangements for existing migrants",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Consultation contemplates transitional arrangements that could temper near-term impact and slow full application by May 2026."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Policy uncertainty and final decisions post-consultation",
        "direction": "neutral",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Final decisions depend on consultation responses; some ambiguity remains about exact application by May 2026."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "We weigh strong official momentum and a clear timetable toward a 10-year baseline as high-probability drivers, tempered by exemptions, transitional rules, and ongoing consultation that create non-uniformity and some near-term uncertainty. The combination yields a high but not absolute likelihood of the 10-year baseline taking effect around May 2026 for a substantial portion of migrants, with variability across cohorts."
  }
}

